6. Explain the four pillars of OOP.

   1. Encapsulation – Wrapping data and methods together and controlling access using access modifiers.
   2. Inheritance – Reusing the properties and behaviour of a parent class.
   3. Polymorphism – One interface or method name can have different implementations.
   4. Abstraction – Hiding implementation details and exposing only required functionality.

