48. What is the difference between BeanFactory and ApplicationContext?

   1. BeanFactory is the basic Spring IoC container.
   2. ApplicationContext provides additional features such as event publishing, internationalisation and application-level integration.
   3. ApplicationContext supports automatic detection of many container-related components.
   4. In most Spring Boot applications, ApplicationContext is used.

