49. Explain @Component, @Service, @Repository and @Controller.

   1. @Component is a generic annotation used to register a class as a Spring bean.
   2. @Service identifies service-layer business logic.
   3. @Repository identifies the persistence layer and supports exception translation.
   4. @Controller identifies Spring MVC controller classes.

