51. Difference between @Primary and @Qualifier.

   1. @Primary identifies the default bean when multiple beans of the same type exist.
   2. @Qualifier selects a specific bean by its qualifier name.
   3. @Primary is useful when one implementation is the default choice.
   4. @Qualifier is useful when we need explicit control over which implementation gets injected.

