52. What is @Configuration and @Bean?

   1. @Configuration marks a class that declares Spring bean definitions.
   2. @Bean marks a method whose returned object should be managed by Spring.
   3. It is useful when configuring third-party classes that we cannot annotate with @Component.
   4. Spring manages the returned object according to its bean lifecycle and scope.

