75. What is an API? How do you design a REST API?

   1. An API allows two software systems to communicate with each other.
   2. I identify the business resource and design resource-based URLs, such as /orders.
   3. I use HTTP methods correctly: GET, POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE.
   4. I include request validation, suitable status codes, error handling, authentication and API documentation.

